 r"I am writing to apply for the Junior Data Scientist I position in the DSaaS team at MarketCast. I am currently completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after graduating from Imperial College London, and I work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have explored large and unfamiliar datasets, built and tested models on them, and then had to explain the result to someone who was going to act on it. I am particularly interested in this role because the work is client-facing analytical research rather than modelling in isolation.",

 r"What attracts me most to MarketCast is the combination of very large behavioural datasets and a team large enough to learn from, with twenty-five or more data scientists already in place. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved. I should say plainly that I have no TV or media industry experience, but the interest is genuine: my most recent work has been on consumer and merchant behaviour, and measuring what actually moves people is the same question I have been asking of health behaviour for the past year.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I mine large-scale merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python to identify growth and operations drivers, and I build KPI frameworks and dashboards that e-commerce teams use to set targets and track initiatives, turning findings into recommendations for operations, product and commercial stakeholders. I also built an AI agent, using Claude Code, that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, and it has been adopted by the wider team and partner teams.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked on a medical AI engagement for a pharmaceutical client. I explored and extracted data from several sources, built a Python pipeline calling six LLM APIs with retrieval and search augmentation which produced and scored more than 2,400 responses, and designed the 246-question benchmark and six-dimension rubric that became the client's acceptance standard. I also mined more than 4,800 consultation threads with a regex and LLM extraction pipeline, and co-built a knowledge graph whose effect on answer quality we tested with blinded paired A/B tests.",

 r"On supervised and unsupervised learning, my MSc dissertation compared logistic regression against three tree ensembles for cardiovascular risk prediction on 458,840 UK Biobank participants, judging them on calibration rather than headline accuracy, and then used doubly robust causal forests to estimate individual-level effects, with overlap weighting, sensitivity analysis including E-values, and external validation in a second cohort. I delivered it as a Streamlit application so that people could run scenarios without touching the code, which I mention because Streamlit and AWS are both in your stack.",

 r"At Ipsos Strategy3 I analysed consumer and healthcare datasets and more than 80 expert interviews, built market-sizing and forecasting models, and produced bespoke client reports and visualisations. This experience has strengthened my ability to document what I did and to present a conclusion to a client rather than a method.",

 r"I should be clear about where I am starting from. Beyond the media-industry gap, my AWS experience is at a basic level and my production engineering experience is limited, so maintaining and improving machine learning pipelines in production is where I would need support early on. My Python, pandas and SQL, my statistics and my ability to take a messy dataset through to a defensible answer are well established.",

 r"I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship. I am based in London and am happy to work across both the London and Reading offices.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in analytics, machine learning and client reporting could support the Data Science team.",
